@{

    ViewData["Title"] = "About";

}

<div class="about-bg">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="about-card">

            <h1 class="about-heading">About BookstaGram</h1>
            <p>

                BookstaGram is a dedicated book‑focused platform designed for readers, donors,

                and book enthusiasts. Our goal is to create a community‑driven reading ecosystem

                that encourages affordability, sustainability, and book circulation.
            </p>

            <h2 class="about-subheading">Problem Statement</h2>
            <p>

                Existing e-commerce platforms do not focus solely on books and lack a

                community-driven exchange system for promoting reading affordability.

                Many readers have unused books but no streamlined platform to donate them

                and get something valuable in return.
            </p>
            <p>

                There is a need for a dedicated and rewards‑based book circulation system

                that encourages reading while minimizing cost.
            </p>

            <h2 class="about-subheading">Proposed Solution</h2>
            <ul class="bullet-list">
                <li>A fully functional book-only e-commerce system.</li>
                <li>Secure user login/registration using ASP.NET Identity.</li>
                <li>A book donation module where users upload details of books they wish to donate.</li>
                @* <li>Virtual coin reward system:</li>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Donate a book → Earn coins</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Use coins for discounts or complete purchase</strong></li>
                </ul> *@
                <li>Clean MVC architecture with modular services.</li>
                <li>Admin dashboard for book management, donation approvals, and coin transactions.</li>
            </ul>

            <p>

                This approach creates a self‑sustaining reading ecosystem where old books

                gain new life.
            </p>

            <h2 class="about-subheading">Team</h2>
            <ul class="bullet-list">
                <li><strong>Backend Development:</strong> Yatendra, Kopal</li>
                <li><strong>Frontend Development:</strong> Deepanshi, Aditya</li>
                <li><strong>Database Management:</strong> Devansh</li>
            </ul>

            <span class="team-badge">We are 5 members</span>

        </div>
    </div>
</div>

